{"title":"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a given point inside quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are located within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b5666ec397ecdd746334b2ec331bf87a176c544d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_1 BC = \\angle ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed33863ca76a9509633a8c1a78f932affb9d1c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_1 CB = \\angle DCP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef11ff304b3c7588cca524bf8a8074289a95dda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_2 AD = \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b0fafe84581126f5255324b948cbab1c21aae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_2 DA = \\angle CDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5920e25e924f4e3b4fd036b98b825eb040dfbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09482ff57fd8b4e8398d0494e4536e4c2c5f8157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae673cfa079c788363f03f09b685855e459bb074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} \\parallel \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"22\" />, then the proof is trivial. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93da5452e7c6d7a4061251746da13cb1c353b72d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{AB} \\cap \\overleftrightarrow{CD} = X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"21\" />. We will show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618412cfa3ecf14e4ae65506d6bf1bd518e81d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{Q_1Q_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"24\" /> passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9b57d19afbd45b10ddcbe272d093fd612eb7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1Q_2} \\not \\parallel \\overline{AB}, \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"22\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is the isogonal conjugate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e450434cd4c8e5a262a81872fce19518921433f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCX$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is the isogonal conjugate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbadd6add0e29b8a87247ea7006168901c183b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADX$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/1912ef0d78690dedd055cb7572074c3bcd22ff09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1, Q_2, X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> lie on the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8a4e9ead6b9180e074141851be2eed80014b6f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${XP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> over the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1b3d6a6ef9474f88d4b0abe3a9e100a94b62fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>-sillybone\n</p><p>-This proof is extremely similar to the one in Evan Chen's <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://web.evanchen.cc/exams/USAMO-2011-notes.pdf\">https://web.evanchen.cc/exams/USAMO-2011-notes.pdf</a>. Please don't sue me.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lemma. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are not parallel, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f44b236cc372858b4adea83e49652454a5fd64a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, CD, Q_1 Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p>Proof. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> meet at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Notice that with respect to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/0/a206569b64a709ee5d59175517dd1a9a6bdeaf3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are isogonal conjugates (this can be proven by dropping altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> depending on where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is). With respect to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1af5442f0ea4c49da55096004a38d0681ca1a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCR$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are isogonal conjugates. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> lie on the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1050dcf31fd5d4e8f36fe23f459b193fa2de9a09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> in the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830c328a4539c236439e2b75cc6faba0b16507da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DRA}$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e7c73e1d5340ee644cb1c06ec3a5b08987e0fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R, Q_1, Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> are collinear. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f44b236cc372858b4adea83e49652454a5fd64a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, CD, Q_1 Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" /> are concurrent at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b95d3628b50966f257d06b97b676dbb201ea11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2 \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"19\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74193a108cf6fc3cd78aa310f9f61d7afca33df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is not parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are not parallel and thus intersect at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74193a108cf6fc3cd78aa310f9f61d7afca33df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> also passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, contradicting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b95d3628b50966f257d06b97b676dbb201ea11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2 \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"19\" />. A similar contradiction occurs if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81455da0edda6d21ca6de293d1a714aa6d2ec7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2 \\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74193a108cf6fc3cd78aa310f9f61d7afca33df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is not parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, so we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b95d3628b50966f257d06b97b676dbb201ea11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2 \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"19\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/81455da0edda6d21ca6de293d1a714aa6d2ec7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 Q_2 \\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5920e25e924f4e3b4fd036b98b825eb040dfbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if the altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are the same, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b700633d95f4d82ae1ce555cf4f0a0118d738a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Q_1B|\\sin \\angle ABQ_1 =|Q_2A|\\sin \\angle BAQ_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"297\" height=\"18\" />.  Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09482ff57fd8b4e8398d0494e4536e4c2c5f8157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022c97930ede830a6ac99d303fbbcb2dd5e0a380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Q_1C|\\sin \\angle DCQ_1 =|Q_2D|\\sin \\angle CDQ_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d46237db3ddf1e620a16db3bcdf8503a8fe37e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S =\\frac{|Q_1B|\\sin \\angle ABQ_1}{|Q_2A|\\sin \\angle BAQ_2} \\times \\frac{|Q_2D|\\sin \\angle CDQ_2}{|Q_1C|\\sin \\angle DCQ_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"343\" height=\"43\" />, then we are done if we can show that S=1.\n</p><p><br />\nBy the law of sines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce264ecc01003e9e1fb707c8be599a6689150c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|Q_1B|}{|Q_1C|}=\\frac{\\sin\\angle Q_1CB}{\\sin\\angle Q_1BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"166\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf52a151b8a8e48cd74fa3ac20fb39ecd797097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|Q_2D|}{|Q_2A|}=\\frac{\\sin\\angle Q_2AD}{\\sin\\angle Q_2DA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"167\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03dfc402539641a21fb730ede2cae45494255752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{\\sin \\angle ABQ_1}{\\sin \\angle BAQ_2}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle CDQ_2}{\\sin \\angle DCQ_1}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle BCQ_1}{\\sin \\angle CBQ_1}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle DAQ_2}{\\sin \\angle ADQ_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"446\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\nBy the terms of the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19324dfa1f987f0fb66f103a6e694a011cb7fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{\\sin \\angle PBC}{\\sin \\angle PAD}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PDA}{\\sin \\angle PCB}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PCD}{\\sin \\angle PBA}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PAB}{\\sin \\angle PDC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"417\" height=\"38\" />.  (If two subangles of an angle of the quadrilateral are equal, then their complements at that quadrilateral angle are equal as well.)   \n</p><p><br />\nRearranging yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a497927f48ad8238641c90d7dc4ac33f06c7564d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S= \\frac{\\sin \\angle PBC}{\\sin \\angle PCB}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PDA}{\\sin \\angle PAD}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PCD}{\\sin \\angle PDC}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin \\angle PAB}{\\sin \\angle PBA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"420\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nApplying the law of sines to the triangles with vertices at P yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5915af75f282358a202f6049ebda77e8915c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{|PC|}{|PB|}\\frac{|PA|}{|PD|}\\frac{|PD|}{|PC|}\\frac{|PB|}{|PA|}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"242\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i><b>Case 1</b></i> The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are not parallel. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03d4d104545b4046337cac72d01399b348d7d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = AB \\cap CD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1e4744af4eda3662fddcfb30a5f56713c59eacc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle Q_1 BC = \\angle ABP, \\angle Q_1 CB = \\angle DCP \\implies\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"16\" />\nPoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> isogonal conjugate of a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d2893bfcf587f3d1bf7e55feba774fee2577bedc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBC \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06175de06075b060abdf04ebd2ecfe88e58fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e693030318a2da2b061f5c9952e73da065aae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EQ_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> are isogonals with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b411f337ac03c8dbf84002e7ad63948e9863dbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Similarly point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> isogonal conjugate of a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with respect to a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6f9805d494e5ce475bdde5e46d977b40099d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EAD \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06175de06075b060abdf04ebd2ecfe88e58fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/30390b274caf05f22048142b92b15585618136f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EQ_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> are isogonals with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b411f337ac03c8dbf84002e7ad63948e9863dbb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Therefore points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4fff1f6ed5b2a4d72177e5b4fc2a83d77b9cc032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, Q_1, Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> lies on the isogonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f06175de06075b060abdf04ebd2ecfe88e58fc97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e283eff855c95c385f1f24e7de6351694728818f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEC \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c9ac19cf814c5807e24128a66b63f0efcd3e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is not parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c918bfa9b7b699552d7779d1de346b73d75010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD.$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><i><b>Case 2</b></i>  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1d79215024e3f73c7a313e8bbda6b612b637c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB||CD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> We use <i><b>The isogonal theorem in case parallel lines</b></i> and get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb862dcb8a4992cf822e0d51849cee186a1aab0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB||Q_1Q_2 || CD. \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\">USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO\" title=\"2011 USAMO\">2011 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.066 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 562/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19077/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.328      1 -total\n 58.75%    9.005      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 38.66%    5.926      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wi